# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.

# Backend base URL INCLUDING its /api prefix. Server-only: the browser never
# sees it — every request goes to this app's /api, which next.config.js proxies
# to the backend so the backend's HttpOnly session cookie lands on this origin.
BACKEND_API_URL=http://localhost:8001/api

# Session token verification (the middleware gating /admin and /pos).
# Server-only, both of them. Each key verifies only its own algorithm, which is
# fixed in code: JWT_ALGORITHM is no longer read here. With both set, both
# kinds of token are accepted; with neither, every token is rejected.
#
# JWT_PUBLIC_KEY  The backend's RS256 public key, the public half of the key it
#                 signs with (SPKI PEM, "-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----"; real
#                 newlines or "\n" both work). It can check a token but never
#                 mint one, so this is the key this app is meant to hold.
# JWT_SECRET      The shared HS256 secret; must match the backend's JWT_SECRET
#                 exactly. A SIGNING key: anything that can read it can mint a
#                 token for any user and role. Only needed until the cutover
#                 below is finished.
#
# Cutover to RS256 (NEX-54), in this order:
#   1. Add JWT_PUBLIC_KEY here, keep JWT_SECRET, and deploy (env changes only
#      reach new deployments). A key that does not parse logs
#      "[auth] JWT_PUBLIC_KEY is not an SPKI PEM public key": fix it before 2.
#   2. Switch the backend to RS256. Until step 4 it can fall back to HS256
#      without touching this app.
#   3. Wait out the 8-hour token lifetime, so no HS256 session is still live.
#   4. Remove JWT_SECRET here and deploy. HS256 tokens stop being accepted.
JWT_SECRET=change-me
# JWT_PUBLIC_KEY="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\n...\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----"

# Content-Security-Policy mode. Leave unset (report-only) until the logs show
# no [csp-report] lines from real traffic, then set "enforce".
# CSP_MODE=enforce

# Hosts product photos are served from (image optimizer allowlist + CSP img-src).
# Defaults to the R2 public bucket; comma-separate to add a custom domain.
# IMAGE_HOSTS=pub-5092fdb36fa84b649893cd173e4339b7.r2.dev
